<title>INDIA: India's Colgate April-August 1996 sales up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>India's Colgate April-August 1996 sales up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colgate-Palmolive India's sales for the first five months of 1996/97 (April-March) were 20 percent higher than the year-ago period, chairman S.A.Lister told shareholders on Wednesday.</p>
<p>He did not give the sales figures.</p>
<p>Colgate-Palmolive India is the Indian subsidiary of the U.S. multinational and is the leader in Indian toothpaste market.</p>
<p>Lister told the annual general meeting that the company would pay a first interim dividend of 16 percent for 1996/97, same as in the year-ago period.</p>
</text>
